  "notes": "Windows-only release. macOS and Linux stay at 2.3.1.\n\n**Download:** `ENG-Drawing-Viewer-2.3.2-Windows-x64-Setup.exe` (Windows 10 1809 or later, or Windows 11, 64-bit). Not code-signed, so SmartScreen may ask once: More info, then Run anyway.\n\n### New\n- **One-file installer.** Installs for your user (no administrator rights), adds a Start menu entry and an optional desktop shortcut, and uninstalls from Settings > Apps.\n- **MARK: select and resize.** Click an annotation to show resize handles. Drag them to resize (hold Shift to keep proportions) or drag the object to move it.\n- **MARK: multiple selection.** Drag a selection rectangle on empty space, or Shift-click to add or remove objects, then move, delete or copy them together.\n- **MARK: copy and paste between drawings.** Ctrl+C copies the selected annotations as editable objects; Ctrl+V pastes them on the same drawing or another one. Pasted callouts continue the numbering and keep their comments. With nothing selected, Ctrl+C still copies the marked page as an image.\n\n`SHA256SUMS.txt` lists the checksums of the installer and the source archive.\n",
